</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">III-B</span>2 </span><span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage-2: Supervised Fine-Tuning with Image Conversation Dataset</span></h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stage 1 yields the <span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reasoning Aligned VLM</span>, tuned for visual reasoning (Fig. <a href="#S1.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ I Introduction ‣ GRPO++: Enhancing Dermatological Reasoning under Low Resource Settings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). While effective at image-based detection, it lacks broader clinical knowledge needed to discuss causes or treatments. To bridge this, we apply <span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT)</span> on an <span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Image Conversation Dataset</span>, producing the <span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conversation Tuned VLM</span>. This equips the model with clinically grounded conversational ability, enabling it to explain diagnoses, discuss etiologies, and suggest treatments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">III-B</span>3 </span><span id="S3.SS2.SSS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage-3: Improving Diagnostic Accuracy via Knowledge Graphs and Preference Tuning</span></h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Dermatologists consult texts, research databases, and guidelines for complex cases, including rare conditions. To reduce hallucination and factual errors, we adopt a Knowledge Graph-based Retrieval-Augmented Generation (KG-RAG). Relevant triples (symptoms, causes, treatments) are retrieved and integrated, grounding responses in validated facts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, continual retrieval increases overhead due to long contexts. To emulate how dermatologists internalize knowledge, we refine Stage-2 with <span id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Direct Preference Optimization (DPO)</span>. An online preference dataset is built from paired outputs: one with KG-RAG (<span id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">chosen</span>) and one without (<span id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rejected</span>). Training with DPO aligns the model to prefer knowledge-grounded answers, internalizing medical patterns while reducing reliance on retrieval. The final model, <span id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DermIQ-VLM</span>, delivers accurate and efficient responses, reflecting a dermatologist’s balance of expertise and practicality (Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ I Introduction ‣ GRPO++: Enhancing Dermatological Reasoning under Low Resource Settings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Theoretical Analysis</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide rigorous theoretical foundations for GRPO++, demonstrating how our confidence-aware modifications address fundamental limitations of standard GRPO while preserving convergence guarantees. We identify two critical failure modes in standard GRPO and establish that our proposed method systematically overcomes these limitations.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Failure Modes of Standard GRPO</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When training models for complex reasoning tasks in low-resource settings—such as generating only a small number of responses per prompt or using smaller language models that tend to produce similar outputs—standard GRPO suffers from two critical failure modes that hinder learning: (i) gradient vanishing due to low response diversity, and (ii) systematic reinforcement of suboptimal behaviors.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span>1 </span>Gradient Vanishing Under Low Diversity</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider response set <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}=\{o_{1},...,o_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}=\{o_{1},...,o_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with rewards <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}=\{r_{1},...,r_{m}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}=\{r_{1},...,r_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. In low diversity regimes—common with small models (&lt;4B parameters) or limited sampling—responses converge such that <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|r_{i}-r_{j}|&lt;\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|r_{i}-r_{j}|&lt;\delta</annotation></semantics></math> for small <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The standard GRPO advantage function:</p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}^{\text{GRPO}}_{i,t}=\frac{r_{i}-\bar{r}}{\sigma_{r}+\varepsilon}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{\text{GRPO}}_{i,t}=\frac{r_{i}-\bar{r}}{\sigma_{r}+\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{r}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j}r_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{r}=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j}r_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{r}=\sqrt{\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j}(r_{j}-\bar{r})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{r}=\sqrt{\frac{1}{m}\sum_{j}(r_{j}-\bar{r})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}\approx r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}\approx r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{A}^{\text{GRPO}}_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{A}^{\text{GRPO}}_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx\frac{r_{c}-r_{c}}{0+\varepsilon}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx\frac{r_{c}-r_{c}}{0+\varepsilon}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This yields vanishing gradients:</p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}=\sum_{i,t}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(o_{i,t}|x)\cdot 0=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO}}=\sum_{i,t}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(o_{i,t}|x)\cdot 0=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Critically, this occurs regardless of whether <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> represents high or low quality, preventing improvement when converged to suboptimal solutions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F3.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.01236v1/figures/worst-same.png" id="S4.F3.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/227;" width="476" height="227" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S4.F3.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Failure mode <a href="#S4.SS1.SSS1" title="IV-A1 Gradient Vanishing Under Low Diversity ‣ IV-A Failure Modes of Standard GRPO ‣ IV Theoretical Analysis ‣ GRPO++: Enhancing Dermatological Reasoning under Low Resource Settings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-A1</span></a> for GRPO in a low-generation setting: repeated identical outputs within a group cause the intra-group advantage to collapse. This is fixed by GRPO++ in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="IV-C Gradient Analysis of GRPO++ ‣ IV Theoretical Analysis ‣ GRPO++: Enhancing Dermatological Reasoning under Low Resource Settings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-C</span></a></span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F3.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.01236v1/figures/worst-diff.png" id="S4.F3.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/227;" width="476" height="227" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S4.F3.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Failure mode <a href="#S4.SS1.SSS2" title="IV-A2 Error Reinforcement Problem ‣ IV-A Failure Modes of Standard GRPO ‣ IV Theoretical Analysis ‣ GRPO++: Enhancing Dermatological Reasoning under Low Resource Settings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-A2</span></a> for GRPO in a low-generation setting: repeated identical outputs within a group cause the intra-group advantage to collapse. This is fixed by GRPO++ in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="IV-C Gradient Analysis of GRPO++ ‣ IV Theoretical Analysis ‣ GRPO++: Enhancing Dermatological Reasoning under Low Resource Settings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-C</span></a></span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Failure mode comparison across GRPO and GRPO++.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span>2 </span>Error Reinforcement Problem</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Even with diversity, when all responses are suboptimal (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}&lt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>), the zero-sum property ensures:</p>
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{m}(r_{i}-\bar{r})=0\implies\exists i^{*}:r_{i^{*}}&gt;\bar{r}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{m}(r_{i}-\bar{r})=0\implies\exists i^{*}:r_{i^{*}}&gt;\bar{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Response <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> receives positive reinforcement despite being suboptimal:</p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}^{\text{GRPO}}_{i^{*},t}=\frac{r_{i^{*}}-\bar{r}}{\sigma_{r}+\varepsilon}&gt;0,\quad r_{i^{*}}&lt;\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mtext>GRPO</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{\text{GRPO}}_{i^{*},t}=\frac{r_{i^{*}}-\bar{r}}{\sigma_{r}+\varepsilon}&gt;0,\quad r_{i^{*}}&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This systematically reinforces inadequate responses, potentially causing convergence on suboptimal solutions.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GRPO++ Solution</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GRPO++ introduces confidence scores based on log-likelihood:</p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}=\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}\log\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(o_{i,t}|q,o_{i,&lt;t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>old</mtext></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}=\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}\log\pi_{\theta_{\text{old}}}(o_{i,t}|q,o_{i,&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For confidence set <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\{i:r_{i}\geq\tau\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\{i:r_{i}\geq\tau\}</annotation></semantics></math>, when <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{C}|=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{C}|=0</annotation></semantics></math> (all suboptimal):</p>
<table id="S4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{A}^{\text{CA}}_{i,t}=-\beta\cdot\frac{\ell_{i}-\ell_{\min}}{\ell_{\max}-\ell_{\min}+\varepsilon}-\gamma" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mtext>CA</mtext></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{\text{CA}}_{i,t}=-\beta\cdot\frac{\ell_{i}-\ell_{\min}}{\ell_{\max}-\ell_{\min}+\varepsilon}-\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are penalty parameters. This ensures <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}^{\text{CA}}_{i,t}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mtext>CA</mtext></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}^{\text{CA}}_{i,t}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">IV-C</span> </span><span id="S4.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Gradient Analysis of GRPO++</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze GRPO++ gradient properties under the suboptimal regime where all responses fail the quality threshold (<math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{C}|=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{C}|=0</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1 (Gradient Vanishing Condition).</span> Under conditions: (i) all responses suboptimal, (ii) <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\max}&gt;\ell_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\max}&gt;\ell_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>, GRPO++ gradients vanish iff <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{m}(\gamma+\beta w_{i})s_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{m}(\gamma+\beta w_{i})s_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> The confidence-aware advantage is:</p>
<table id="S4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{i}=-\gamma-\beta w_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{i}=-\gamma-\beta w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=(\ell_{i}-\ell_{\min})/(\ell_{\max}-\ell_{\min}+\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=(\ell_{i}-\ell_{\min})/(\ell_{\max}-\ell_{\min}+\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The gradient becomes:</p>
<table id="S4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO++}}=-\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}(\gamma+\beta w_{i})s_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO++</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO++}}=-\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}(\gamma+\beta w_{i})s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Vanishing requires the weighted sum of score functions to equal zero. Unlike standard GRPO, this condition depends on both confidence weights <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and policy gradients <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2 (Gradient Bounds).</span> Let <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\max}=\max_{i}\|s_{i}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\max}=\max_{i}\|s_{i}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{\min}=\min_{i}\|s_{i}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{\min}=\min_{i}\|s_{i}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Under no perfect cancellation:</p>
<table id="S4.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\gamma+\frac{\beta}{m}\right)G_{\min}\leq\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO++}}\|\leq\left(\gamma+\frac{(m-1)\beta}{m}\right)G_{\max}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO++</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\gamma+\frac{\beta}{m}\right)G_{\min}\leq\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO++}}\|\leq\left(\gamma+\frac{(m-1)\beta}{m}\right)G_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> Apply triangle inequality: <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO++}}\|\leq\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}|\hat{A}_{i}|\|s_{i}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>GRPO++</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{J}_{\text{GRPO++}}\|\leq\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i=1}^{m}|\hat{A}_{i}|\|s_{i}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{A}_{i}|=\gamma+\beta w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{A}_{i}|=\gamma+\beta w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the constraint <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\max}&gt;\ell_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\max}&gt;\ell_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> prevents all <math id="S4.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> simultaneously.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Upper bound:</span> Extremal case with <math id="S4.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-1)</annotation></semantics></math> responses having <math id="S4.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, one with <math id="S4.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{(m-1)(\gamma+\beta)+\gamma}{m}G_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{(m-1)(\gamma+\beta)+\gamma}{m}G_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\gamma+\frac{(m-1)\beta}{m}\right)G_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\gamma+\frac{(m-1)\beta}{m}\right)G_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Lower bound:</span> Extremal case with one response having <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-1)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\nabla\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\nabla\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{(\gamma+\beta)+(m-1)\gamma}{m}G_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{(\gamma+\beta)+(m-1)\gamma}{m}G_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\gamma+\frac{\beta}{m}\right)G_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\gamma+\frac{\beta}{m}\right)G_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The derived bounds are <span id="S4.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">provably tight</span>, as they can be achieved under specific extremal conditions. The upper bound is attained when the confidence distribution places <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-1)</annotation></semantics></math> responses at <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and one at <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>, with all score vectors aligned constructively. Conversely, the lower bound is realized when one response is at <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and the remaining <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-1)</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>, with minimal destructive interference. Moreover, the <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{\beta}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{\beta}{m}</annotation></semantics></math> corrections emerge from the structural constraint that it is fundamentally impossible for all <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to equal <math id="S4.SS3.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> simultaneously.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F4.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01236v1/training_comparison_mean_combined_reward_1.svg" id="S4.F4.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/281;" width="476" height="281"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F4.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S4.F4.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">GRPO vs GRPO++ (Qwen2-VL-2B)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F4.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01236v1/training_comparison_mean_combined_reward_2.svg" id="S4.F4.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/281;" width="476" height="281"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F4.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S4.F4.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">GRPO vs GRPO++ (Qwen2.5-VL-3B)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reward comparison across GRPO and GRPO++.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">V </span><span id="S5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experiments and Results</span></h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We built a custom benchmark of 138 unseen image pairs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> from DermNetNZ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, with <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>20 images per class, to evaluate dermatological disease detection.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">V-A</span> </span><span id="S5.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experimental Setup</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage-1: GRPO++</span>, training used two 15GB T4 GPUs with 4-bit quantization and LoRA to reduce memory and computation. LoRA (rank=32, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>=64, dropout=0.05) targeted <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">q_proj</span>, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">k_proj</span>, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">v_proj</span>, and <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">o_proj</span>. Training ran for <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>1700 steps (10 epochs) with learning rate <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size 1 (4 grad accumulation), and temperature 0.9. Generation parameters were set to 3 for both 2B and 3B models. For <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage-2: Fine-Tune</span> and <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage-3: DPO</span> (Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ I Introduction ‣ GRPO++: Enhancing Dermatological Reasoning under Low Resource Settings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), 4-bit quantization and LoRA were again used (rank=8, <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>=16, dropout=0.05), expanding targets to include <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">down_proj</span>, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">up_proj</span>, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gate_proj</span>, etc. Training used <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> learning rate, 2 epochs, batch size 1 (2 grad accumulation), AdamW (weight decay=0.01), linear scheduler (warmup=0.03), and gradient clipping (0.3).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span> </span><span id="S5.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines and Metrics</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DermIQ-VLM was compared against Qwen2.5-VL-2B/3B-Instruct. For detection, answers between <span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;answer&gt;</span>…<span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/answer&gt;</span> were matched to ground truth; majority voting aggregated predictions for robustness.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Conversation quality was judged by Grok and GPT-4, checking adherence to <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;thinking&gt;</span>…<span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/thinking&gt;</span> and <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;answer&gt;</span>…<span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;/answer&gt;</span> formats. Metrics included <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">factual accuracy</span> (disease correctness), <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">relevance</span> (query alignment), and <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">completeness</span> (coverage of reasoning and diagnosis).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">V-C</span> </span><span id="S5.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Detected Disease Reward:</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This reward guides the model toward accurate, clinically safe diagnoses by combining general reward constants (Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ V-C Detected Disease Reward: ‣ V Experiments and Results ‣ GRPO++: Enhancing Dermatological Reasoning under Low Resource Settings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>) with a severity-based penalty matrix (Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ V-C Detected Disease Reward: ‣ V Experiments and Results ‣ GRPO++: Enhancing Dermatological Reasoning under Low Resource Settings" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a>). Correct predictions earn a base reward, while errors incur penalties scaled by clinical risk. For example, misclassifying Melanoma or cancerous disease as Dermatitis or inflamatory disease yields a severe penalty of <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-5.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-5.0</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas confusing Actinic Keratosis with Seborrheic Keratosis incurs only <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2.0</annotation></semantics></math>. Additional rules handle invalid predictions, unknown ground truth, and default mismatches.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T1" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S5.T1.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:79.1pt;vertical-align:-36.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(39.1pt,-9.0pt) scale(1.29334353596798,1.29334353596798) ;">
<table id="S5.T1.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T1.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T1.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter Description</span></th>
<th id="S5.T1.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T1.3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T1.3.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Base reward for correct disease identification</td>
<td id="S5.T1.3.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+10.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>10.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+10.0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.3.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Penalty for failing to output a valid disease</td>
<td id="S5.T1.3.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-5.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-5.0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.3.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.3.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Penalty if ground truth label is unknown/invalid</td>
<td id="S5.T1.3.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.5</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.3.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.3.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Default penalty for unlisted misclassifications</td>
<td id="S5.T1.3.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2.5</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE I</span>: </span><span id="S5.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">General reward and penalty constants.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S5.T2.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:107.6pt;vertical-align:-51.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(16.7pt,-5.2pt) scale(1.1072875844169,1.1072875844169) ;">
<table id="S5.T2.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T2.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">True Disease</span></th>
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">AK</th>
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">BCC</th>
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Derm.</th>
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Mel.</th>
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Psor.</th>
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Ros.</th>
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.1.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">SK</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T2.3.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">AK</th>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">N/A</td>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">-1.0</td>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">-3.0</td>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">-1.5</td>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">-3.0</td>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">-3.0</td>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.2.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">-2.0</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.3.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T2.3.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">BCC</th>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">-1.5</td>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">N/A</td>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">-4.0</td>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">-2.0</td>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.3.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">-4.0</td>
<td id="S5.T2.3.1.3.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">-4.0</td>
